                <pb facs="0494" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg382"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Dawson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-03-23"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                    1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram of March 19. Colombian minister for foreign affairs says that he
                    believes when the assembly approves the treaty with Panama it will adopt a
                    resolution declaring that “Region of Jurado” does not extend south of Jurado
                    River. He says such a resolution would enormously facilitate Government’s labors
                    to secure approval. Desires your opinion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
